 In a previous article, acolvin@youth.cavebbs.gen.nz (Aaron Colvin) writes:
>Well, after reading a message from Holger Joist awhile back that 
> ad ae ar um = secret door to treasure room, I was surprised when I found 
>such a message written on the floor about 30 moves after starting again from 
>scratch.. (ad ae?ar um is what I got actually),

If you are an experienced player, skip this stuff.  If you are new and want
a few pointers, read on.....


Yes, you will find the original message as posted, but as you walk over it a
couple of times, you will scuff it out and it will only show as question marks.
Eventually, it will be totally obliterated.  (I think you will note that the
message is 'written in the Dust', or something like that).

>I searched for doors (naturally), and found one straight away, it was a 1 uare 
>passage to no-where, but after further serching I found another exit, and 
>after entering that I found myself in a 2x2 room of gold...of course, having 
>just started (using Valkyrie), I didnt have a wand of digging or anything of 
>the like, and I was stuck there, after awhile the guard came in, and asked 
>me my name, I entered in what I thought Holger said, but I fear I spelt it 
>wrong, as the reply from the guard was 'I do not know you ... etc'

It's pretty pointless to enter the treasure room without a pick axe or some
method to teleport out.  A wand of digging will help too.  If you do find such
a room, make sure to drop all your current gold before you go into the teleport
trap.  Otherwise, you have to drop it too and will loose it until you can dig
back in with a pick axe.  I think the proper answer to get the guard to leave
you alone is 'Croesus' (without quotes, of course) but this just makes the
guard go away and you are still stuck in the room.  He will come back later
and ask you again if you do this.

> And I had to drop my gold and follow him, but when I am confronted with 
>situations similar to this I try to battle my way out of it, which of course 
>was a useless situation, resulting in an instantaneous death...
> As to what happens when one follows the guard, I dunno.. Does anybody know 
>what happens when you do as the guard says?

It's tough to kill a guard (I haven't done it) and is not possible until you
get to higher levels of skill.  Just drop the gold in the room (all of it!)
and follow him as he leads you back into the rest of the maze.  As you follow
him, the path you leave will close up behind you and seal the room.  You have
to dig back into it later.

